      "lineNbr": 173,
      "author": {
        "id": 18384
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T12:16:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, but also this is a pointer, and it isn\u0027t meant to \"own\" the memory.\n\nIf we called `sk_free(fPtr)`, this would free memory, but immediately trigger the dangling pointer detector because `fPtr` is now dangling.\n\nThere is an escape hatch with:\n```\nsk_free(fPtr.ExtractAsDangling())\n```\n\nthat \"move\" the pointer value out of the raw_ptr and pass it to `sk_free`, while keeping the MiraclePtr protection during the current line scope.\n\nIdeally, we would turn the pointer into smart pointer.\n\nI addressed this in:\nhttps://skia-review.git.corp.google.com/c/skia/+/1408757",
      "parentUuid": "f26e9f17_2f61b6df",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 173,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 173,
        "endChar": 42
      },
